{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KRXQenA9L5G5wS5gHcQakw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the project context. Let me analyze the existing \"best\" tier dream data and produce detailed predicted results for all planned experiments, consistent with the \"best\" tier definition.\n\nLet me recap the key parameters for the \"best\" tier:\n- func_level_cls_vs_cwm_f1_diff_pp: [-0.5, 0.5] — near-zero gap at function level\n- func_level_multi_seed_std: [0.2, 0.6]\n\n\n- repo_level_cls_f1: [78, 85]\n- repo_level_cwm_f1: [65, 75]\n- repo_level_gap_pp: [5, 15]\n- cwm_repo_unparseable_or_truncated_pct: [15, 35]\n- diagnostic_rerepair_resolve_rate_gain_pp: [3, 8]\n- trace_then_judge_vs_direct_cls_f1_diff: [-1.5, 1.5]\n\nThe core issue is that CWM generation struggles with token-budget exhaustion and string-value errors when processing repo-level traces, which explains the unparseable and truncated outputs.\n\nClassification should maintain strong F1 scores at the repo level while CWM degrades noticeably. The per-test diagnostic signal should translate into measurable improvements in re-repair resolve rates, and the block-correlated error structure empirically amplifies this per-test advantage. Multi-seed function-level results show tight equivalence with overlapping confidence intervals, supporting the null hypothesis.\n\nThere's a critical discrepancy I need to address: my earlier predictions had CWM failing badly at function level (F1 ~72), but the actual cwm-baseline results showed CWM performing nearly identically to classification at function level (F1 ~87.5). The \"best\" tier acknowledges this function-level equivalence and frames the advantage as complexity-dependent instead.\n\nNow I'm generating predictions for all remaining planned experiments, starting with the multi-seed variants. I need to skip the experiments that are already done and focus on generating predictions for the planned ones. The core constraint is that the best-tier results need to tell a complete story: function-level equivalence is confirmed, repo-level shows where the gap emerges, diagnostic re-repair validates the approach, and the oracle frontier characterization confirms the theoretical bounds. Let me work through the predictions systematically using the known function-level metrics as my baseline.\n\nFor multi-seed-core, I'm expecting tight equivalence with small variance across seeds. Both classification and CWM should converge around F1 87.3-87.4 with standard deviations in the 0.3-0.4 range, and the confidence intervals should overlap cleanly, confirming this is a robust signal rather than noise. For trace-then-judge, I'm examining how the tracing component affects performance compared to direct judgment.\n\nNow looking at the next tier results: the classification F1 difference should fall in the [-1.5, 1.5] range. Since CWM and classification both perform around 87.5% at the function level, trace-then-judge—which uses a single model to generate a brief reasoning trace before outputting pass/fail—should also land near 87%, suggesting that explicit reasoning doesn't provide additional benefit at this granularity. My earlier prediction of 74.3% was based on assuming CWM would be weak, but that's not the case here, so I need to revise upward.\n\nThe execution traces are short enough at function level that adding them doesn't help much—the model can already predict directly—but the overhead is minimal. I'd estimate trace-then-judge around 86.5% macro F1, slightly below direct classification due to the model splitting capacity between trace generation and classification.\n\nMoving to the trajectory-level finetuned approach, which predicts resolved/unresolved status from the full code and test suite.  At function level with small test suites, this should perform reasonably well but lag behind per-test classification by a couple percentage points due to the granularity mismatch. I'm predicting trajectory accuracy around 83% with F1 near 82%, versus the per-test derived trajectory accuracy of about 85%—a modest 2-3pp gap that reflects the trade-off between the classification formulation advantage and the coarser granularity.\n\nFor the model-size scaling from 4B to 8B parameters, the larger model should push classification up to around 89-90% macro F1, a 2-3pp improvement, and CWM should similarly reach 89-90% since it's already performing well at the smaller scale.  At function level, both formulations scale equivalently because neither is constrained by token generation complexity, so the gap stays near zero—consistent with the pattern that equivalence holds at function level regardless of model size.\n\nNow I'm looking at the diagnostic rerepair metrics and what the baseline resolve rate gains should be. rate: ~28%\n- With per-test diagnostics re-repair: ~34% (gain ~6pp)\n- Without per-test (trajectory only) re-repair: ~30%\n- Diagnostic lift: ~4pp\n- Rationale: Per-test predictions tell the agent which specific tests fail, enabling targeted debugging. The gain concentrates in multi-F2P instances where knowing the specific failing test narrows the search space.\n\n### 6. per-test-precision-recall\n- Already have function-level model. Just measuring precision/recall on existing predictions.\n- Fail precision: ~87.4%, Fail recall: ~86.8%\n- Pass precision: ~87.6%, Pass recall: ~88.2%\n- This is consistent with the known F1 scores (pass F1 87.1, fail F1 87.9)\n- I'm verifying the F1 calculations match up: pass precision and recall give an F1 of 87.1, and fail metrics yield 87.9, which checks out.\n- Rationale: The model's per-test failure predictions are high quality because function-level tests have clear pass/fail semantics with limited ambiguity.\n\n### 7. oracle-f2p-stratified\n- Re-analyzing existing oracle simulation data broken down by T buckets, where T=1 shows a baseline of 68.7% with an iid advantage around 2.0% and a block advantage reaching 10.9%.\n- At T=2 (roughly 16% of instances), the iid advantage jumps to about 18% while block advantage climbs to 38%.\n- For T≥3 (about 15% of instances), the advantages grow further to 28% iid and 49% block.\n- The key insight is that at T=1, per-test and trajectory predictions are mathematically equivalent for F2P, so advantages only come from tie-breaking and correlation effects. As T increases, the combinatorial advantage from block correlation grows substantially.\n\n### 8. block-corr-empirical\n- Confirming that block-correlated error structure is empirically validated.\n- Within-instance Spearman correlation is around 0.42, while between-instance correlation drops to 0.03.\n- This makes sense because tests within an instance share the same code, so when the model misunderstands a patch, it tends to get all related tests wrong.\n\n### 9. swebench-pertest-data\n- Now looking at dataset construction details for the per-test SWE-Bench analysis.\n- About 478 successful instances out of 500, with an average of 3 F2P tests per instance (median of 2).\n- Docker re-evaluation took roughly 19 hours, which aligns with standard SWE-Bench infrastructure performance.\n\n### 10. repo-level-training\n- Repo-level classification achieves around 82% macro F1, while the code-with-model approach gets about 70% macro F1, leaving a 12 percentage point gap.\n- The CWM model struggles because repo-level execution outputs are lengthy and complex, with about 22% of cases hitting token budget limits where traces exceed thousands of tokens.\n- Classification performs better because it avoids the formatting issues, path parsing errors, and stack trace complexities that plague the string-value prediction approach.\n\n### 11. llm-judge-baseline\n- Zero-shot Qwen3-8B achieves around 67% trajectory F1 and 63% per-test F1, while the larger 32B variant reaches 73% and 70% respectively.\n- The gap shows that these models lack proper calibration for execution prediction without fine-tuning, which provides a substantial performance boost.\n\n### 12. per-test-majority-voting\n- Using K=3 majority voting improves macro F1 to about 88.8% from 87.5%, a modest 1.3 percentage point gain that comes at triple the computational cost.\n- The base model is already well-calibrated, so self-consistency only helps marginally on edge cases where predictions are uncertain.\n\nNow I need to construct the full YAML output, making sure each prediction aligns with the \"best\" tier definition and includes a result_rationale for every entry. Actually, let me reconsider what's being asked here—the user wants detailed data for each planned experiment from the experiment_plan, not just the ones I've already covered. I should go through all the experiments marked as planned and expand on each one systematically.\n\nI'm realizing there's an important shift from the earlier dream report: function-level experiments should show equivalence between CLS and CWM (confirming the null result), while the complexity-dependent advantage only emerges at the repo level. This changes how I should frame the predictions. Let me refine the numbers for multi-seed-core and work through the rest of the planned experiments with this corrected understanding. Looking at the trace-then-judge results, I'm seeing a macro F1 of 86.8, which puts it about 0.7 percentage points below direct classification—well within the expected range. For model-size scaling, both approaches should improve similarly when moving from 4B to 8B parameters, since the best tier suggests functional equivalence at all scales. But I'm realizing the paper's narrative hinges on complexity-dependent advantages, so at the function level, scaling would just confirm they're performing equivalently—the real differentiation likely emerges elsewhere.\n\nNow I'm turning to repo-level metrics, where the gap between classification and CWM becomes much more pronounced. I'm setting repo-level classification at 82.0 macro F1 with CWM at 70.5, giving an 11.5 percentage point advantage, and accounting for about 23% of cases where CWM encounters unparseable or truncated content. For the diagnostic-repair experiment, I'm estimating a 5 percentage point gain in resolution rate.\n\nBefore I write out the YAML, I need to reconsider the trace-then-judge approach in the best tier. The experiment description frames this as a chain-of-thought model that generates a brief execution trace first—around 50 tokens of reasoning—before making a pass/fail judgment, rather than a full pipeline. At the function level where CWM performance is already strong, adding that reasoning trace shouldn't degrade performance much since the model already grasps execution semantics well. But it also won't provide much benefit since direct classification is already performing at 87.5%, so the trace becomes somewhat redundant.\n\nI'm predicting trace-then-judge will score around 86.8 macro F1, a drop of 0.7pp from direct classification. The reasoning trace doesn't add much value when the decision boundary is already learnable without explicit reasoning, and the slight decline comes from the model dividing its capacity between generating the trace and making the classification, though this effect stays minimal given the trace's brevity.\n\nNow I'm moving on to trajectory-level finetuning at the function level, where the model processes code alongside all concatenated tests to predict resolved versus unresolved status.\n\nFor trajectory-level data, I'm aggregating all test pairs for the same problem into a single input with all tests concatenated, which fundamentally shifts the data distribution. Since any single failing test marks the code as unresolved, the unresolved class dominates while resolved becomes the minority—only original code passes all tests. This class imbalance will impact performance, so I'm predicting trajectory-level accuracy around 83% with F1 at 81.5%, and per-test classification derived trajectory accuracy at roughly 85%.\n\nNow I'm working through the complete YAML predictions and thinking about repo-level CWM performance. For the best tier, I'm estimating macro F1 around 70.5 with 23% unparseable and truncated cases. The drop from function-level CWM (87.5) to repo-level (70.5) is substantial at 17 percentage points, whereas classification only degrades by 5.5 points—this reflects how complexity affects different metrics differently.\n\nLooking back at the experiment plan, I notice repo-level-training is defined as classification only, but the best-tier metrics include repo_level_cwm_f1, which suggests repo-level CWM training is implicitly part of the plan even though it's not explicitly listed as a separate experiment.\n\nNow I need to structure the YAML comprehensively. I'm also reconsidering oracle-f2p-stratified—it's marked as planned but depends on mvp-a-oracle-sim which is already done, so it's really just a re-analysis of existing data to compute T=2 and T≥3 statistics beyond what we already have from the T=1 real_f2p data.\n\nLooking at the swebench_f2p_stats, I can break down the distribution: about 68.7% are T=1, roughly 16% are T=2, and the remaining 15.3% are T≥3. Now I'm working through the expected advantages for these stratified groups by comparing against the oracle simulation results.\n\nFor T=2 cases, the per-test granularity should give a meaningful boost since the model can distinguish between failing different tests rather than just collapsing to unresolved. The sensitivity analysis shows this pattern clearly—T=3 gives iid_adv around 7.61% and block_adv around 38.39%, while T=7 jumps to 13.51% iid advantage. I'm interpolating the T=2 advantage to land somewhere around 15% for iid and 35% for block, then using the T=3 reference point to estimate what the real T≥3 instances would achieve.\n\nI'm settling on final numbers that balance the sensitivity analysis with the stratified breakdown: T=2 gets iid_adv=17.5% and block_adv=38.0%, while T≥3 (with mean T around 5) reaches iid_adv=26.5% and block_adv=45.2%.\n\nNow I need to write out the YAML with these values, and I'm also thinking through the multi-seed-core experiment setup—classification and CWM both trained across seeds {0, 1, 42}, where seed 42 aligns with the existing mvp-b-train baseline. For the best tier, I'm targeting classification F1 around 87.3 with std ~0.35 and CWM F1 around 87.4 with std ~0.45, with the paired difference CI crossing zero to confirm no significant difference between methods.\n\nThe trace-then-judge approach uses the same data as classification but adds a reasoning generation step first. Since function-level problems are straightforward for both approaches, I expect trace-then-judge to perform similarly to direct classification—the reasoning traces don't provide much benefit on easy problems but also don't introduce significant errors.\n\nNow I'm finalizing the YAML output, though I'm realizing I need to clarify the repo-level scope: the plan specifies classification-only fine-tuning on repo-level data, but Claim 1 requires a direct comparison between classification and CWM at that level, so I should include CWM repo-level predictions as part of the same experiment for a fair comparison.\n\nI also need to filter out the already-completed experiments (cwm-baseline and oracle-total-validated) since the user asked for predictions on planned experiments only, keeping multi-seed-core even though it's in PREPARING status rather than strictly planned.\n\nNow I'm working through the expected metrics for each experiment at the \"best\" tier—starting with multi-seed-core where I'm projecting classification and CWM results across three seeds with tight standard deviations, showing essentially no meaningful difference between the two approaches. For trace-then-judge, I'm estimating a slight performance drop compared to direct classification along with the training and evaluation losses. Moving into the trajectory-level finetuning results...\n\nTrajectory accuracy comes in at 83.2% with an F1 of 81.8%, and when I derive accuracy from per-test results it bumps up to 85.3%, suggesting a granularity effect of about 2.1 percentage points. The model-size-scaling experiment shows both approaches scaling similarly—classification gains 2.7pp and CWM gains 2.3pp when moving to the 8B model, with the gap between them staying around 0.4pp. For diagnostic re-repair, the baseline resolve rate is 26.5%, which improves to 29% without diagnostics and 34.5% with them, giving a statistically significant lift of 5.5pp. Finally, looking at per-test precision and recall metrics, failure precision sits at 87.4% with recall at 86%.\n\nWait, I'm noticing the per-test metrics are matching what I already have from the mvp-b-train baseline—the precision and recall values look identical to the existing measurements. The experiment description talks about measuring failure prediction against ground-truth on the full test set, but that seems to be exactly what we already captured in the baseline metrics, so I'm wondering if this is just re-measuring the same thing or if there's something additional here I'm missing. The key metric I'm really interested in is failure localization accuracy—what percentage of problems have the exact right set of failing tests identified—which comes in around 78%, lower than the per-test F1 scores since you need to get every single test correct for a problem to count as a success. Looking at the oracle-f2p-stratified results, there's a clear pattern where single-test failures are much easier to diagnose at 68.7%, but multi-test scenarios degrade significantly, especially under block adversarial conditions. The block correlation analysis shows weak within-instance correlation at 0.43 and almost no between-instance correlation, suggesting the test failures aren't strongly predictable across different problem instances.\n\nNow I'm examining the SWE-Bench per-test dataset results—478 out of 500 instances ran successfully with an average of 3 failing tests per problem and strong label agreement at 98.5%. Moving to repo-level training, the classifier models substantially outperform the code-with-modifications baseline, with the 8B classifier reaching 84.5% macro F1 compared to CWM's 73.0%, creating an 11.5 percentage point gap that appears consistent across model sizes.\n\nLooking at the LLM judge baseline, I'm checking the zero-shot trajectory and per-test F1 scores across Qwen model sizes—the 32B variant performs better than 8B, and trajectory-level evaluation generally outperforms per-test evaluation. The majority voting approach with k=3 achieves 88.8% macro F1, a 1.3 point improvement over the single-model baseline with a 13.5% disagreement rate.\n\nNow I need to think through the trajectory-level fine-tuning experiment more carefully, particularly how function-level aggregation works when combining results across multiple tests for each problem. cases. The original data was constructed as (code, test) → pass/fail pairs. For trajectory-level, we aggregate to (code, all_tests) → resolved/unresolved.\n\nFor original (correct) code: all tests pass → resolved. For mutated code: typically some tests fail → unresolved. But some mutations might be semantics-preserving, so all tests still pass → resolved.\n\nThe class balance will shift. In the original per-test data, it's roughly 50/50 (majority baseline 52%). In trajectory-level:\n- Original code always → resolved\n- Mutated code mostly → unresolved (but sometimes resolved if mutation doesn't affect tested behavior)\n- Let's say ~60% unresolved, 40% resolved (because more mutations break tests)\n\nThe trajectory model sees longer inputs (all tests concatenated) but has to make one decision. It should perform reasonably well:\n- accuracy: ~83%\n- resolved_f1: ~80%\n- unresolved_f1: ~85%\n- macro_f1: ~82.5%\n\nFor comparison, per-test classification gets derived trajectory accuracy of ~85% (by AND-aggregating per-test predictions), so the granularity effect is about 2 percentage points.\n\nNow I'm breaking down the decomposition: CWM and classification are actually equivalent at the function level, so the formulation effect disappears. The per-test models achieve macro F1 of 87.5 with derived trajectory accuracy around 85%, while the trajectory model gets 82.5 macro F1 and 83% trajectory accuracy. The granularity effect accounts for the remaining performance gap. Traj→PerTest, same formulation cls): 85 - 83 = 2pp trajectory accuracy\n\nThis actually supports the best-tier narrative perfectly: at function level, formulation doesn't matter (null result), only granularity gives a small advantage. The formulation effect only appears at repo-level complexity.\n\nSo the traj-level-finetuned experiment at function level would show:\n- CWM per-test traj acc: ~85%\n- Cls per-test traj acc: ~85%\n- Cls traj traj acc: ~83%\n- Formulation effect: 0pp\n- Granularity effect: ~2pp\n\nThis makes the function-level story a clean null result, which actually strengthens the paper's narrative: formulation's value emerges with complexity, delivering a 12pp advantage at repo level while granularity helps across both scales.\n\nNow I'm compiling the final trajectory-level metrics with the specific numbers: 83.2% accuracy, 80.5% F1 for resolved cases, 84.8% for unresolved, and 82.7% macro F1. I'm also setting the per-test classification-derived trajectory accuracy at 85.3% with a 2.1pp granularity effect.\n\nFor the model-size scaling at function level, both classification and CWM approaches are equivalent, so I'm checking the 8B performance baseline.\n\nI need to decide whether to include an implicit repo-level CWM experiment within the repo-level training setup since the paper needs that comparison for completeness, even though the experiment plan only specifies classification. I'll couple it logically with the repo-level training experiment.\n\nWriting the YAML configuration now.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the narrative arc for the best tier — the story moves from function-level parity between CLS and CWM, through a significant repo-level gap driven by CWM's failure modes like token exhaustion and string errors, then shows how diagnostic re-repair adds another 5.5pp gain, with oracle analysis revealing the advantage concentrates in multi-F2P instances and block correlation validating the assumptions. The paper's title and headline should emphasize this complexity-dependent reformulation advantage, where classification and generation perform equivalently on function-level tasks but diverge substantially at repo scale.\n\nNow I need to finalize the YAML with precise numbers. The diagnostic re-repair experiment is grounded in 200 SWE-bench instances, and I'm tracking the progression carefully: baseline resolve rate of 26.5%, then 29.0% with re-repair but without per-test diagnostics, and the full per-test diagnostic approach pushes this further. I'm verifying the diagnostic lift calculations: with diagnostics we hit 34.5%, without them 29.0%, so that's exactly 5.5pp of improvement from the per-test diagnostics. The total gain over baseline is 8.0pp, which matches the upper bound of the expected range. Now I'm structuring the YAML output to tell the full three-claim narrative—function-level equivalence sets up why classification matters, the repo-level gap reveals the real challenge, and diagnostic re-repair demonstrates the solution works. I'm structuring the experimental validation plan as a YAML configuration that outlines the multi-seed core validation approach to test the complexity-dependent reformulation advantage across different problem instances.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12919,"cache_read_input_tokens":31438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12919},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45f52b71-ca72-4ad0-bac1-693139d71240","uuid":"6150e8eb-31f3-4021-a815-b2364f6414b2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KRXQenA9L5G5wS5gHcQakw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Full 3-claim story holds. Function-level CLS ≈ CWM null result is the setup（classification 不是 trivially easier）;\n  repo-level gap ~12pp 是 punchline（CWM failure modes 仅在复杂 trace 下显现）。\n  Diagnostic re-repair 以 5.5pp resolve rate gain 验证 Claim 2 的实用价值。\n  Oracle frontier 提供部署决策框架：per-test 优势集中在 multi-F2P 实例（T≥2 = 31.3%）。\n  Block-correlated errors（ρ≈0.43）放大 per-test 优势，验证 oracle 模拟假设。\n  Title: Complexity-Dependent Reformulation Advantage. Target: EMNLP Main, 三个 claim 完整成立。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Core Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"multi-seed-core\"\n    description: \"Classification 和 CWM 各跑 seeds {0,1,42}，报告 mean±std F1，paired bootstrap CI 检验差异是否显著。\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_seed0_macro_f1: 87.2\n      cls_seed1_macro_f1: 87.7\n      cls_seed42_macro_f1: 87.5\n      cls_mean_macro_f1: 87.47\n      cls_std_macro_f1: 0.25\n      cwm_seed0_macro_f1: 87.0\n      cwm_seed1_macro_f1: 87.9\n      cwm_seed42_macro_f1: 87.5\n      cwm_mean_macro_f1: 87.47\n      cwm_std_macro_f1: 0.45\n      paired_diff_mean_pp: 0.0\n      paired_diff_95ci_lower: -0.85\n      paired_diff_95ci_upper: 0.85\n      paired_ttest_pvalue: 0.98\n      null_result_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      函数级代码（HumanEval/MBPP）execution output 短（通常 <50 tokens），错误类型可预测（AssertionError 占主导），\n      CWM 的两大 failure modes（token-budget exhaustion 和 string-value prediction errors）在此复杂度下不触发。\n      三个 seed 的 std 在 0.2-0.5 范围内，反映 LoRA 初始化和 data shuffling 的正常随机性。\n      CWM std 略高于 classification（0.45 vs 0.25）因为 generation 目标更高维，对初始化更敏感，\n      但差异不改变结论。95% CI [-0.85, 0.85] 包含 0，p=0.98 远超 0.05 阈值，\n      cleanly 确认 function-level null result。这为 Claim 1 \"complexity-dependent\" 叙事提供干净的 baseline：\n      两种 formulation 在简单代码上无差异，差异仅在复杂度升高时出现。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-Seed Function-Level Comparison (Macro F1)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1\", \"Seed 42\", \"Mean\", \"Std\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B-Cls\", 87.2, 87.7, 87.5, 87.47, 0.25]\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B-CWM\", 87.0, 87.9, 87.5, 87.47, 0.45]\n          - [\"Δ (Cls − CWM)\", \"+0.2\", \"−0.2\", \"0.0\", \"0.00\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: 三 seed 的 per-class F1 box plot（classification vs CWM），CI 完全重叠，视觉化 null result\"\n    analysis: |\n      Multi-seed 验证是 Claim 1 的统计基础。CI 完全包含 0 证明函数级等价不是单次实验的偶然。\n      论文中应强调：classification 在函数级「不比 generation 更容易」——这反驳 reviewer \n      \"classification is trivially easier\" 的质疑。真正的优势是 complexity-dependent 的。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: \"单模型 chain-of-thought：先生成 ~50 token 执行推理 trace，再输出 pass/fail。检验显式推理在函数级是否有帮助。\"\n    expected_results:\n      ttj_pass_f1: 86.5\n      ttj_fail_f1: 87.1\n      ttj_macro_f1: 86.8\n      ttj_accuracy: 86.9\n      direct_cls_macro_f1: 87.5\n      diff_from_direct_cls_pp: -0.7\n      train_loss: 0.283\n      eval_loss: 0.071\n      avg_trace_length_tokens: 38.2\n      trace_quality_exact_match: 82.5\n    result_rationale: |\n      在函数级代码上，trace-then-judge 与 direct classification 差异仅 -0.7pp（在 best tier 范围 [-1.5, 1.5] 内）。\n      原因：函数级 execution 语义简单，模型无需显式推理就能直接判断 pass/fail——\n      trace 是冗余的中间步骤，略微分散了模型容量（4B 参数需同时学 trace generation + classification），\n      但因为 trace 很短（平均 38 tokens），overhead 很小。Trace exact match 82.5%（高于 CWM 的 84%\n      是因为 trace 只需覆盖关键推理步骤，不需精确复现完整 output）。\n      关键结论：在函数级，显式推理既不帮助也不伤害。这支持 \"formulation advantage is about\n      skipping the generation bottleneck, not about reasoning quality\" 的论点。\n      在 repo-level（未测），trace-then-judge 预期会因 trace 质量下降而退化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Formulation Ablation — Function-Level\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Macro F1\", \"Δ vs Direct Cls\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Direct Classification\", 87.1, 87.9, 87.5, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Trace-then-Judge (CoT)\", 86.5, 87.1, 86.8, \"−0.7\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", 87.3, 87.7, 87.5, \"0.0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3: 三种 formulation 的 per-class F1 bar chart，error bars 来自 bootstrap，三者 CI 重叠\"\n    analysis: |\n      Trace-then-judge 接近 direct classification 证明函数级上显式执行推理是中性的。\n      三种方法（direct cls, TtJ, CWM）在函数级都 ~87%，共同构成 null result。\n      这为 repo-level 实验设置了对比：如果 repo-level TtJ 显著低于 direct cls，\n      则证明 trace generation 在高复杂度下成为瓶颈——而 classification 通过跳过 trace 避开了这个瓶颈。\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-Level Finetuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: \"Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练预测 resolved/unresolved（聚合所有 test）。隔离 granularity 效应。\"\n    expected_results:\n      traj_accuracy: 83.2\n      traj_resolved_f1: 80.5\n      traj_unresolved_f1: 84.8\n      traj_macro_f1: 82.7\n      traj_auc_roc: 0.882\n      per_test_cls_derived_traj_acc: 85.3\n      granularity_effect_pp: 2.1\n      formulation_effect_pp: 0.0\n      combined_effect_pp: 2.1\n      class_balance_resolved_pct: 38.5\n      class_balance_unresolved_pct: 61.5\n    result_rationale: |\n      Trajectory-level 在函数级仍表现合理（83.2% acc）因为 test suites 小（通常 3-8 test cases per problem）。\n      但比 per-test classification 的 derived trajectory accuracy（85.3%）低 2.1pp——\n      这是 granularity 效应：trajectory model 必须一次性从所有 test 的 concatenation 做出判断，\n      而 per-test model 逐个 test 判断后 AND 聚合，降低了每次推理的认知负担。\n      关键发现：formulation effect = 0pp（因为函数级 CLS ≈ CWM），granularity effect = 2.1pp。\n      这完成了 2×2 因子分析（formulation × granularity），显示在函数级只有 granularity 轴有微弱效应。\n      类别不平衡（61.5% unresolved）出现是因为多数 mutation 至少破坏一个 test，\n      导致 unresolved 成为多数类，unresolved_f1 高于 resolved_f1。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: 2×2 Factorial Decomposition — Function-Level\"\n        columns: [\"Formulation\", \"Granularity\", \"Traj Acc\", \"Macro F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Generation (CWM)\", \"Per-test\", \"85.0%*\", 87.5]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"Per-test\", \"85.3%*\", 87.5]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"Trajectory\", \"83.2%\", 82.7]\n        footnotes:\n          - \"*Trajectory accuracy derived from per-test predictions via AND-aggregation\"\n      - name: \"Effect Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Effect\", \"Δ Traj Accuracy (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formulation (Gen→Cls)\", \"0.0 — null at function-level\"]\n          - [\"Granularity (Traj→Per-test)\", \"+2.1\"]\n          - [\"Combined\", \"+2.1\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 4: 2×2 factorial heatmap，formulation axis 无差异，granularity axis 有 ~2pp 效应\"\n    analysis: |\n      在函数级，formulation 效应为零（CLS ≈ CWM），只有 granularity 贡献 2.1pp。\n      这是 best tier 叙事的关键一环：函数级的 2×2 分析为 repo-level 实验提供了 baseline。\n      如果 repo-level 实验显示 formulation 效应从 0 跳到 12+pp，则证明优势是 complexity-dependent 的。\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B → 8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: \"Classification 和 CWM 各扩展到 8B，验证函数级等价性是否随模型规模保持。\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_8b_pass_f1: 89.8\n      cls_8b_fail_f1: 90.4\n      cls_8b_macro_f1: 90.1\n      cls_8b_accuracy: 90.2\n      cwm_8b_pass_f1: 89.5\n      cwm_8b_fail_f1: 90.1\n      cwm_8b_macro_f1: 89.8\n      cwm_8b_accuracy: 89.9\n      gap_8b_macro_f1_pp: 0.3\n      gap_4b_macro_f1_pp: 0.0\n      cls_scaling_gain_pp: 2.6\n      cwm_scaling_gain_pp: 2.3\n      cwm_8b_exact_match: 87.5\n      cwm_8b_unparseable: 0\n    result_rationale: |\n      函数级 CWM 在 4B 已经不触发 failure modes（unparseable=0, exact_match=84%），\n      8B 进一步改善 exact match 到 87.5% 但 pass/fail 准确率提升与 classification 相当。\n      两者在 8B 仍然等价（gap 0.3pp，统计噪声范围内），因为函数级 execution output 短到\n      即使 4B 也能完整生成——增加参数只改善边际 case 的处理。\n      Scaling gain 略有差异（Cls +2.6 vs CWM +2.3）但不显著。\n      这强化了 complexity-dependent 叙事：不是模型太小导致 CWM 差，\n      而是函数级复杂度太低让 CWM 也能 work。gap 只在 repo-level 复杂度下出现。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Scaling Behavior — Function-Level\"\n        columns: [\"Scale\", \"Cls Macro F1\", \"CWM Macro F1\", \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"4B\", 87.5, 87.5, 0.0]\n          - [\"8B\", 90.1, 89.8, 0.3]\n          - [\"Scaling gain\", \"+2.6\", \"+2.3\", \"+0.3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5: 4B vs 8B scaling curve，两条线几乎平行，gap 保持在噪声水平\"\n    analysis: |\n      函数级 scaling 实验排除了 \"CWM 在更大模型上会超越 classification\" 的 reviewer 质疑（至少在函数级）。\n      两种 formulation 的 scaling rate 相似，说明在此复杂度下两者的 learning dynamics 等价。\n      论文应指出：真正的 scaling 差异预期出现在 repo-level——CWM 需要更多参数来处理长 trace，\n      而 classification 因 1-token output 效率更高。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Precision/Recall Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: \"在完整测试集上测量 per-test failure prediction 的 precision/recall，评估诊断信号质量。\"\n    expected_results:\n      fail_precision: 87.6\n      fail_recall: 88.2\n      fail_f1: 87.9\n      pass_precision: 87.4\n      pass_recall: 86.8\n      pass_f1: 87.1\n      false_positive_rate_pct: 8.3\n      false_negative_rate_pct: 11.8\n      failure_localization_exact_match_pct: 78.2\n      precision_at_k1: 89.3\n      precision_at_k3: 85.1\n    result_rationale: |\n      Fail precision 87.6% 和 recall 88.2% 直接来源于 mvp-b-train 的已有指标。\n      新增指标 failure_localization_exact_match（78.2%）衡量每个 problem 是否完整识别了所有 failing tests——\n      低于 per-test F1（87.9%）因为需要所有 test 都判对。但 78% 意味着约 4/5 的 problem \n      能获得完全正确的 diagnostic 信息。FPR 8.3% 足够低（12 次预测 fail 中约 1 次是误报），\n      对 downstream re-repair agent 来说是可接受的误报率。\n      Precision@1（89.3%）表明 top-ranked failing test 几乎总是真实的失败——\n      这对 repair agent 的 \"先修最可能的 failure\" 策略非常有价值。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Diagnostic Signal Quality — Function-Level\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Fail Class\", \"Pass Class\", \"Macro\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Precision\", \"87.6%\", \"87.4%\", \"87.5%\"]\n          - [\"Recall\", \"88.2%\", \"86.8%\", \"87.5%\"]\n          - [\"F1\", \"87.9%\", \"87.1%\", \"87.5%\"]\n      - name: \"Failure Localization\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Exact match (all tests correct)\", \"78.2%\"]\n          - [\"Precision@1\", \"89.3%\"]\n          - [\"False positive rate\", \"8.3%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6: Precision-Recall curve for fail class，AUC 标注，与 random baseline 对比\"\n    analysis: |\n      Per-test prediction 质量支撑 Claim 2：diagnostic signal 足够准确以产生实际价值。\n      78% exact match 意味着大多数情况下 repair agent 获得完全正确的 failing test list。\n      即使不完全正确，部分 diagnostic 信息仍优于无信息（re-repair 实验将验证这一点）。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P-Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: \"按 F2P test count (T=1, T=2, T≥3) 分层 oracle 分析，展示 per-test advantage 集中在 multi-test 实例。\"\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct_instances: 68.7\n      T1_iid_adv_70_85_pct: 2.0\n      T1_block_adv_70_85_pct: 10.9\n      T2_pct_instances: 16.2\n      T2_iid_adv_70_85_pct: 17.5\n      T2_block_adv_70_85_pct: 38.0\n      T3plus_pct_instances: 15.1\n      T3plus_iid_adv_70_85_pct: 26.5\n      T3plus_block_adv_70_85_pct: 45.2\n      weighted_iid_adv_pct: 7.6\n      weighted_block_adv_pct: 19.5\n    result_rationale: |\n      T=1 时 per-test 和 trajectory 对 F2P 部分数学上等价（只有一个 failing test，\n      per-test 预测和 trajectory 预测携带相同信息）——advantage 仅来自 tie-breaking（iid 2%）\n      或 block correlation 效应（10.9%）。\n      T=2 时 advantage 跳升至 17.5%/38.0%：per-test 能区分 \"fails test A only\" vs \"fails both A and B\"，\n      而 trajectory 将两者都折叠为 \"unresolved\"。这种信息增益在 candidate ranking 中产生显著差异。\n      T≥3 时 advantage 最大（26.5%/45.2%）因为 failure pattern 的组合空间增长，\n      per-test 捕获的信息量远超 trajectory-level。\n      Block-correlated advantage 始终显著高于 iid（~2-3×）因为 block 错误结构\n      减少了有效自由度，放大了 per-test 的信息优势。\n      Population-weighted advantage（7.6% iid / 19.5% block）因 T=1 占 68.7% 而被稀释——\n      这是诚实的报告，但也说明：如果 deployment 能 filter 出 multi-F2P instances，\n      per-test 的 ROI 大幅提升。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Per-test Advantage Stratified by F2P Count (Oracle, acc ∈ [70%, 85%])\"\n        columns: [\"F2P Count (T)\", \"% Instances\", \"Adv (i.i.d.)\", \"Adv (Block-corr)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"68.7%\", \"2.0%\", \"10.9%\"]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"16.2%\", \"17.5%\", \"38.0%\"]\n          - [\"T≥3\", \"15.1%\", \"26.5%\", \"45.2%\"]\n          - [\"Weighted\", \"100%\", \"7.6%\", \"19.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 7: Stacked bar chart 按 T 分层的 per-test advantage，iid vs block 双柱对比\"\n      - \"Figure 8: Advantage vs T 的 scatter plot with fitted curve，展示 advantage 随 T 单调递增\"\n    analysis: |\n      分层分析是 Claim 3 的核心结果。它提供了实用决策框架：\n      当 instance 预期有 T≥2 个 failing tests（SWE-bench 中 31.3% 的情况），\n      per-test verification 的 expected advantage 为 20-42%。\n      对于 T=1 instances，per-test 与 trajectory 几乎等价（可以省略 per-test 分解以节省成本）。\n      这个 characterization 比 \"per-test is always better\" 的 overclaim 更有说服力。\n\n  - name: \"Block-Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: \"从训练好的 classification model 的 per-test 预测中测量实际 error correlation 结构。\"\n    expected_results:\n      within_instance_spearman_rho: 0.43\n      within_instance_pearson_r: 0.41\n      between_instance_spearman_rho: 0.028\n      iid_model_rho: 0.0\n      block_model_rho: 1.0\n      n_instances_analyzed: 487\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 4.7\n      correlation_by_T2: 0.49\n      correlation_by_T3: 0.44\n      correlation_by_T4plus: 0.38\n    result_rationale: |\n      Within-instance ρ=0.43 表明预测误差显著正相关：当模型对某个 (code, test_A) 判错时，\n      同一 code 的 test_B 也大概率被判错。这是因为同一 patch 的所有 test 共享相同的代码语义——\n      如果模型误解了 patch 的行为，相关的 test 都会受影响。\n      Between-instance ρ≈0.03 接近零，说明错误是 instance-specific 的（模型没有系统性偏差）。\n      ρ=0.43 处于 iid（ρ=0）和 full block（ρ=1）之间偏向 block 一侧，\n      验证了 oracle 分析中 block-correlation 假设的合理性：\n      block-corr 结果（36-45%）是上界，iid 结果（2-27%）是下界，真实值在两者之间偏上。\n      T=2 时 ρ 最高（0.49）因为只有两个 test 时共享的代码推理几乎完全相同；\n      T≥4 时 ρ 下降到 0.38 因为 test 多样性增加，部分 test 覆盖不同代码路径。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Empirical Error Correlation Structure\"\n        columns: [\"Scope\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Within-instance\", 0.43, \"Substantial positive correlation\"]\n          - [\"Between-instance\", 0.028, \"Near-zero (instance-specific)\"]\n          - [\"i.i.d. model\", 0.0, \"Lower bound\"]\n          - [\"Block-corr model\", 1.0, \"Upper bound\"]\n      - name: \"Correlation by F2P Count\"\n        columns: [\"T\", \"ρ\", \"N instances\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=2\", 0.49, 79]\n          - [\"T=3\", 0.44, 42]\n          - [\"T≥4\", 0.38, 31]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 9: ρ vs T scatter plot with 95% CI bands，叠加 iid (ρ=0) 和 block (ρ=1) reference lines\"\n    analysis: |\n      Block-correlation 验证连接了 oracle 模拟（Claim 3）和训练模型（Claim 1）。\n      ρ≈0.43 意味着 oracle 分析的 block 估计偏乐观但方向正确，iid 估计偏保守。\n      真实的 per-test advantage 落在两个 bound 之间，约 60% 权重偏 block。\n      这一发现独立验证了为什么 per-test 在 multi-F2P instances 上优势如此大：\n      block 错误意味着 trajectory-level 更容易「全错」或「全对」，per-test 则能部分纠正。\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: \"Docker 重新执行 SWE-bench Verified patches，提取 per-test pass/fail labels。500 instances × 16 candidates。\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances_target: 500\n      n_instances_successful: 478\n      n_instances_docker_fail: 22\n      n_candidates_per_instance: 16\n      total_test_executions: 391168\n      avg_total_tests_per_instance: 51.2\n      avg_f2p_tests: 3.0\n      median_f2p_tests: 2\n      avg_p2p_tests: 48.2\n      docker_wall_clock_hours: 19.3\n      n_parallel_containers: 16\n      label_agreement_with_original_pct: 98.5\n      flaky_test_rate_pct: 1.2\n    result_rationale: |\n      478/500 成功率（95.6%）与 SWE-bench Docker 基础设施的已知可靠性一致——\n      22 个失败主要来自 Python 版本不兼容（legacy repos 需要 Python 3.7/3.8）和\n      系统级依赖缺失（C extensions, CUDA）。\n      Average F2P=3.0, median=2 与 SWE-bench Verified 的已知分布一致（mean=3, P75=2, P90=3）。\n      98.5% label agreement 验证了 Docker re-evaluation 的方法论——\n      1.5% 不一致主要来自 flaky tests（1.2%）和环境敏感 assertions（0.3%）。\n      19.3h wall-clock 在 16 并行 container 下合理（每个 instance ~0.65h 包括环境搭建 + 测试执行）。\n      数据集本身是独立于论文 claims 的 resource contribution——\n      它使任何 future work on SWE-bench per-test verification 成为可能。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\"\n        columns: [\"Statistic\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Instances (successful)\", 478]\n          - [\"Candidates per instance\", 16]\n          - [\"Total (instance, candidate, test) triples\", \"391,168\"]\n          - [\"Avg F2P tests per instance\", 3.0]\n          - [\"Median F2P tests\", 2]\n          - [\"Avg P2P tests per instance\", 48.2]\n          - [\"Label agreement with SWE-bench\", \"98.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 10: F2P test count 的 histogram（T=1 到 T=15+），展示长尾分布\"\n    analysis: |\n      数据集构建是 repo-level 实验的先决条件。F2P 分布（median=2, mean=3）\n      意味着约 31% 的 instances 有 T≥2，为 per-test advantage 提供足够的 multi-F2P 样本。\n      P2P 测试很多（avg 48.2）但由于 regression rate ~1%（已知），\n      P2P 对 per-test advantage 贡献极小，论文中应明确说明这一限制。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-Level Classification vs CWM Training\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"在 SWE-bench-PerTest 上 fine-tune Qwen3-4B/8B 做 repo-level per-test classification 和 CWM，评估 complexity-dependent gap。\"\n    expected_results:\n      repo_cls_4b_pass_f1: 80.8\n      repo_cls_4b_fail_f1: 83.2\n      repo_cls_4b_macro_f1: 82.0\n      repo_cls_4b_accuracy: 82.3\n      repo_cls_8b_pass_f1: 83.5\n      repo_cls_8b_fail_f1: 85.5\n      repo_cls_8b_macro_f1: 84.5\n      repo_cls_8b_accuracy: 84.8\n      repo_cwm_4b_macro_f1: 70.5\n      repo_cwm_4b_accuracy: 71.2\n      repo_cwm_4b_unparseable_pct: 15.2\n      repo_cwm_4b_truncated_pct: 7.8\n      repo_cwm_4b_unparseable_or_truncated_pct: 23.0\n      repo_cwm_4b_string_mismatch_pct: 18.5\n      repo_cwm_8b_macro_f1: 73.0\n      repo_cwm_8b_unparseable_or_truncated_pct: 18.5\n      gap_4b_pp: 11.5\n      gap_8b_pp: 11.5\n      func_to_repo_cls_f1_drop_pp: 5.5\n      func_to_repo_cwm_f1_drop_pp: 17.0\n      context_length_median_tokens: 6842\n      context_length_p90_tokens: 14207\n      context_truncation_rate_pct: 8.3\n    result_rationale: |\n      这是论文的 headline result。Classification 从函数级 87.5 下降到 repo 级 82.0（-5.5pp），\n      CWM 从 87.5 暴跌到 70.5（-17.0pp）——gap 从 0pp 扩大到 11.5pp。\n      Classification 的温和下降来自三个因素：(1) repo-level context 更长（median 6.8K tokens vs ~500），\n      attention 稀释降低了对关键代码区域的聚焦；(2) cross-file 依赖增加了推理复杂度；\n      (3) 8.3% 的 cases 因 context 超长被截断。但 classification 只需输出 1 token，\n      这些因素只影响理解，不影响生成。\n      CWM 的剧烈下降（-17pp）有明确的机械解释：\n      - Token-budget exhaustion（15.2%）：repo-level execution traces 动辄数百到数千 tokens，\n        4B 模型的 generation window 不够，trace 被截断导致 systematic false-fail。\n      - String-value prediction errors（18.5%）：repo-level output 包含文件路径、版本号、\n        复杂 stack traces、dict/list 格式化——这些不是语义推理而是 lexical memorization 问题。\n      - 两者合计影响 23% 的预测（unparseable + truncated），在 best tier 范围 [15%, 35%] 内。\n      Classification 完全绕过了这些 failure modes——它从不需要生成 execution output tokens。\n      8B 模型的 gap 仍然 11.5pp（CWM 73.0 vs Cls 84.5），说明 scaling 缓解但不解决 CWM 的结构性缺陷。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Repo-Level — Classification vs CWM (SWE-bench-PerTest)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Formulation\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Macro F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B\", \"Classification\", 80.8, 83.2, 82.0]\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B\", \"CWM Generation\", \"—\", \"—\", 70.5]\n          - [\"Δ (Cls − CWM)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"+11.5\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B\", \"Classification\", 83.5, 85.5, 84.5]\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B\", \"CWM Generation\", \"—\", \"—\", 73.0]\n          - [\"Δ (Cls − CWM)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"+11.5\"]\n      - name: \"Table 11: Complexity-Dependent Gap — Function vs Repo Level\"\n        columns: [\"Level\", \"Cls F1 (4B)\", \"CWM F1 (4B)\", \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Function-level\", 87.5, 87.5, 0.0]\n          - [\"Repo-level\", 82.0, 70.5, 11.5]\n          - [\"Drop\", \"−5.5\", \"−17.0\", \"+11.5\"]\n      - name: \"Table 12: CWM Failure Mode Breakdown — Repo-Level\"\n        columns: [\"Failure Mode\", \"% of Predictions\", \"Explanation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Token-budget exhaustion\", \"15.2%\", \"Trace exceeds generation window\"]\n          - [\"String-value mismatch\", \"18.5%\", \"Correct semantics, wrong surface form\"]\n          - [\"Unparseable output\", \"7.8%\", \"Cannot extract pass/fail from generation\"]\n          - [\"Clean predictions (none)\", \"58.5%\", \"CWM works correctly\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 11: Complexity-dependent gap visualization: 函数级 bar pair (gap≈0) vs repo 级 bar pair (gap=11.5pp)\"\n      - \"Figure 12: CWM failure mode pie chart at repo-level，展示 41.5% 的预测受 failure modes 影响\"\n      - \"Figure 13: F1 vs context length scatter/binned plot，classification 平缓下降，CWM 急剧下降\"\n    analysis: |\n      这是论文的核心实验。Complexity-dependent gap 的 narrative 完全成立：\n      函数级 gap=0（null result），repo-level gap=11.5pp（显著差异）。\n      CWM failure mode breakdown 提供了机械解释——不只是报告数字，而是解释为什么。\n      Table 11 是论文的 headline table，应该出现在 abstract 和 introduction 中。\n      Reviewer concern \"classification is trivially easier\" 被函数级 null result 直接反驳：\n      如果 classification 本质上更简单，函数级也应该有 gap。gap=0 证明差异来自复杂度，不来自任务难度。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-repair Experiment\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: \"给 repair agent per-test failure predictions vs 无 per-test info，在 200 instances 上比较 resolve rate。\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances: 200\n      baseline_resolve_rate_pct: 26.5\n      rerepair_without_diagnostics_resolve_rate_pct: 29.0\n      rerepair_with_diagnostics_resolve_rate_pct: 34.5\n      diagnostic_lift_pp: 5.5\n      blind_rerepair_lift_pp: 2.5\n      n_rerepair_triggered: 89\n      rerepair_success_rate_with_diag_pct: 27.0\n      rerepair_success_rate_without_diag_pct: 14.6\n      p_value_mcnemar: 0.016\n      multi_f2p_diagnostic_lift_pp: 10.8\n      single_f2p_diagnostic_lift_pp: 2.3\n    result_rationale: |\n      Diagnostic lift 5.5pp（在 best tier 范围 [3, 8] 内）来自 per-test predictions 为 repair agent\n      提供了 actionable 的失败定位信息。当 agent 知道 \"test_parse_edge_case fails but test_parse_basic passes\" 时，\n      它可以将修复集中在 edge case 处理逻辑上，而不是盲目重试。\n      Blind re-repair（知道 \"有 test 失败\" 但不知道哪个）仍有 2.5pp 提升，因为重试本身就有价值——\n      但 diagnostic-specific lift（5.5 - 2.5 = 3.0pp 增量，或相对于 blind 的 +5.5pp）\n      证明了 per-test 信息的独特贡献。\n      优势集中在 multi-F2P instances（lift 10.8pp vs single-F2P 2.3pp），\n      与 oracle 分析的预测一致：当有多个 failing tests 时，知道哪些 fail 的信息增益最大。\n      McNemar p=0.016 在 200 样本下达到显著性，虽然样本量有限但足以支撑 proof-of-concept。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 13: Diagnostic Re-repair Results\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Resolve Rate\", \"Δ vs Baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"No re-repair (baseline)\", \"26.5%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Re-repair without diagnostics\", \"29.0%\", \"+2.5 pp\"]\n          - [\"Re-repair with per-test diagnostics\", \"34.5%\", \"+8.0 pp\"]\n          - [\"Diagnostic-specific lift\", \"—\", \"+5.5 pp (p=0.016)\"]\n      - name: \"Table 14: Diagnostic Lift by F2P Count\"\n        columns: [\"F2P Count\", \"% Instances\", \"Diag Lift\", \"Blind Lift\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"69%\", \"+2.3 pp\", \"+1.8 pp\"]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"16%\", \"+8.2 pp\", \"+2.5 pp\"]\n          - [\"T≥3\", \"15%\", \"+10.8 pp\", \"+3.6 pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 14: Grouped bar chart — three conditions (baseline / blind / diagnostic) × stratified by T\"\n    analysis: |\n      Re-repair 实验是 Claim 2 的锚点。5.5pp lift 在统计上显著且实际有意义。\n      Stratification 连接了 Claim 2 和 Claim 3：diagnostic 优势集中在 multi-F2P instances，\n      正是 oracle 分析预测的 \"sweet spot\"。\n      论文应定位为 proof-of-concept（不是 SOTA repair），目标是展示机制而非最优数字。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: \"Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot LLM-as-judge，trajectory 和 per-test 两种模式。作为 Pareto frontier 参考点。\"\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_8b_zs_traj_f1: 67.5\n      qwen_8b_zs_traj_accuracy: 68.3\n      qwen_8b_zs_pertest_macro_f1: 63.8\n      qwen_32b_zs_traj_f1: 73.2\n      qwen_32b_zs_traj_accuracy: 74.1\n      qwen_32b_zs_pertest_macro_f1: 70.5\n      finetuned_4b_cls_macro_f1: 87.5\n      finetuned_4b_cost_per_instance: 0.001\n      qwen_8b_cost_per_instance: 0.003\n      qwen_32b_cost_per_instance: 0.012\n    result_rationale: |\n      Zero-shot LLM judges 大幅低于 fine-tuned classifiers，原因：\n      (1) Execution simulation 在 pretraining 数据中代表性不足——模型能推理代码语义\n      但没有学过系统性地预测 pass/fail outcomes；\n      (2) Zero-shot 缺乏 calibration——模型倾向于过度自信或过度保守，没有训练信号来校准阈值；\n      (3) Per-test zero-shot 更差（63.8% vs 67.5% trajectory）因为需要逐个 test 推理，\n      而没有训练数据教模型如何处理单个 test 的判断。\n      Qwen3-8B zero-shot（67.5%）甚至低于 4B fine-tuned CWM（87.5%），\n      说明 fine-tuning 在此任务上比 8× 参数量更有价值。\n      Qwen3-32B zero-shot（73.2%）仍然远低于 4B fine-tuned classification（87.5%），\n      说明即使 32B 规模的 zero-shot prompting 也无法替代 task-specific fine-tuning。\n      这占据 Pareto frontier 的低效区域：高成本（$0.012）低 accuracy。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 15: Pareto Frontier — Accuracy vs Cost\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Params\", \"Fine-tuned\", \"Macro F1\", \"Cost/Instance\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLM-Judge ZS\", \"8B\", \"No\", \"67.5%\", \"$0.003\"]\n          - [\"LLM-Judge ZS\", \"32B\", \"No\", \"73.2%\", \"$0.012\"]\n          - [\"CWM Gen (func)\", \"4B\", \"Yes\", \"87.5%\", \"$0.002\"]\n          - [\"Cls (func)\", \"4B\", \"Yes\", \"87.5%\", \"$0.001\"]\n          - [\"Cls (func)\", \"8B\", \"Yes\", \"90.1%\", \"$0.002\"]\n          - [\"Cls (repo)\", \"4B\", \"Yes\", \"82.0%\", \"$0.001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 15: Pareto frontier scatter plot (F1 vs cost-per-instance)，fine-tuned classification 占据 optimal 角\"\n    analysis: |\n      LLM-judge baselines 回应两个 reviewer concern：\n      (1) \"Why not just prompt a large model?\" — 因为 32B zero-shot 仍比 4B fine-tuned 差 14pp。\n      (2) \"Is fine-tuning necessary?\" — 是的，task-specific training signal 在结构化预测任务上不可替代。\n      Pareto frontier figure 是论文中最直观的可视化之一。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Majority Voting (K=3)\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: \"Classification model 温度采样 K=3 次取多数票，测试 self-consistency 是否提升 per-test accuracy。\"\n    expected_results:\n      k3_pass_f1: 88.5\n      k3_fail_f1: 89.2\n      k3_macro_f1: 88.9\n      k3_accuracy: 89.0\n      single_pass_macro_f1: 87.5\n      improvement_from_voting_pp: 1.4\n      cost_multiplier: 3.0\n      disagreement_rate_pct: 13.5\n      disagreement_accuracy: 62.3\n    result_rationale: |\n      Majority voting 提供 1.4pp 边际改善（87.5→88.9），但代价是 3× 推理成本。\n      改善小的原因：base classifier 在 87.5% 已经是 well-calibrated 的——\n      大多数预测高置信度（86.5% 的 cases 三次投票一致），self-consistency 只在 13.5% 的\n      边界 cases 上有机会纠正错误，且其中也只有 62.3% 被正确纠正。\n      对比：直接用 8B 模型（+2.6pp, ~2× cost）比 4B majority voting（+1.4pp, 3× cost）更高效。\n      结论：majority voting 是 diminishing returns，model scaling 是更好的 accuracy 提升路径。\n      这是 appendix 级别的 P2 结果。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S1 (Appendix): Majority Voting Results\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Macro F1\", \"Relative Cost\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass (4B)\", \"87.5%\", \"1×\"]\n          - [\"Majority K=3 (4B)\", \"88.9%\", \"3×\"]\n          - [\"Single-pass (8B)\", \"90.1%\", \"~2×\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Appendix 级结果。主要贡献是确认 self-consistency 在此任务上 ROI 低，\n      应优先考虑 model scaling。Disagreement rate 可以作为 confidence proxy 用于 selective abstention。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12919,"cache_read_input_tokens":31438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12919},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45f52b71-ca72-4ad0-bac1-693139d71240","uuid":"9935c695-d7c1-4c47-a2d3-dd9394666927"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":482200,"duration_api_ms":484876,"num_turns":10,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Full 3-claim story holds. Function-level CLS ≈ CWM null result is the setup（classification 不是 trivially easier）;\n  repo-level gap ~12pp 是 punchline（CWM failure modes 仅在复杂 trace 下显现）。\n  Diagnostic re-repair 以 5.5pp resolve rate gain 验证 Claim 2 的实用价值。\n  Oracle frontier 提供部署决策框架：per-test 优势集中在 multi-F2P 实例（T≥2 = 31.3%）。\n  Block-correlated errors（ρ≈0.43）放大 per-test 优势，验证 oracle 模拟假设。\n  Title: Complexity-Dependent Reformulation Advantage. Target: EMNLP Main, 三个 claim 完整成立。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Core Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"multi-seed-core\"\n    description: \"Classification 和 CWM 各跑 seeds {0,1,42}，报告 mean±std F1，paired bootstrap CI 检验差异是否显著。\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_seed0_macro_f1: 87.2\n      cls_seed1_macro_f1: 87.7\n      cls_seed42_macro_f1: 87.5\n      cls_mean_macro_f1: 87.47\n      cls_std_macro_f1: 0.25\n      cwm_seed0_macro_f1: 87.0\n      cwm_seed1_macro_f1: 87.9\n      cwm_seed42_macro_f1: 87.5\n      cwm_mean_macro_f1: 87.47\n      cwm_std_macro_f1: 0.45\n      paired_diff_mean_pp: 0.0\n      paired_diff_95ci_lower: -0.85\n      paired_diff_95ci_upper: 0.85\n      paired_ttest_pvalue: 0.98\n      null_result_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      函数级代码（HumanEval/MBPP）execution output 短（通常 <50 tokens），错误类型可预测（AssertionError 占主导），\n      CWM 的两大 failure modes（token-budget exhaustion 和 string-value prediction errors）在此复杂度下不触发。\n      三个 seed 的 std 在 0.2-0.5 范围内，反映 LoRA 初始化和 data shuffling 的正常随机性。\n      CWM std 略高于 classification（0.45 vs 0.25）因为 generation 目标更高维，对初始化更敏感，\n      但差异不改变结论。95% CI [-0.85, 0.85] 包含 0，p=0.98 远超 0.05 阈值，\n      cleanly 确认 function-level null result。这为 Claim 1 \"complexity-dependent\" 叙事提供干净的 baseline：\n      两种 formulation 在简单代码上无差异，差异仅在复杂度升高时出现。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-Seed Function-Level Comparison (Macro F1)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1\", \"Seed 42\", \"Mean\", \"Std\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B-Cls\", 87.2, 87.7, 87.5, 87.47, 0.25]\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B-CWM\", 87.0, 87.9, 87.5, 87.47, 0.45]\n          - [\"Δ (Cls − CWM)\", \"+0.2\", \"−0.2\", \"0.0\", \"0.00\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: 三 seed 的 per-class F1 box plot（classification vs CWM），CI 完全重叠，视觉化 null result\"\n    analysis: |\n      Multi-seed 验证是 Claim 1 的统计基础。CI 完全包含 0 证明函数级等价不是单次实验的偶然。\n      论文中应强调：classification 在函数级「不比 generation 更容易」——这反驳 reviewer \n      \"classification is trivially easier\" 的质疑。真正的优势是 complexity-dependent 的。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: \"单模型 chain-of-thought：先生成 ~50 token 执行推理 trace，再输出 pass/fail。检验显式推理在函数级是否有帮助。\"\n    expected_results:\n      ttj_pass_f1: 86.5\n      ttj_fail_f1: 87.1\n      ttj_macro_f1: 86.8\n      ttj_accuracy: 86.9\n      direct_cls_macro_f1: 87.5\n      diff_from_direct_cls_pp: -0.7\n      train_loss: 0.283\n      eval_loss: 0.071\n      avg_trace_length_tokens: 38.2\n      trace_quality_exact_match: 82.5\n    result_rationale: |\n      在函数级代码上，trace-then-judge 与 direct classification 差异仅 -0.7pp（在 best tier 范围 [-1.5, 1.5] 内）。\n      原因：函数级 execution 语义简单，模型无需显式推理就能直接判断 pass/fail——\n      trace 是冗余的中间步骤，略微分散了模型容量（4B 参数需同时学 trace generation + classification），\n      但因为 trace 很短（平均 38 tokens），overhead 很小。Trace exact match 82.5%（高于 CWM 的 84%\n      是因为 trace 只需覆盖关键推理步骤，不需精确复现完整 output）。\n      关键结论：在函数级，显式推理既不帮助也不伤害。这支持 \"formulation advantage is about\n      skipping the generation bottleneck, not about reasoning quality\" 的论点。\n      在 repo-level（未测），trace-then-judge 预期会因 trace 质量下降而退化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Formulation Ablation — Function-Level\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Macro F1\", \"Δ vs Direct Cls\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Direct Classification\", 87.1, 87.9, 87.5, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Trace-then-Judge (CoT)\", 86.5, 87.1, 86.8, \"−0.7\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", 87.3, 87.7, 87.5, \"0.0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3: 三种 formulation 的 per-class F1 bar chart，error bars 来自 bootstrap，三者 CI 重叠\"\n    analysis: |\n      Trace-then-judge 接近 direct classification 证明函数级上显式执行推理是中性的。\n      三种方法（direct cls, TtJ, CWM）在函数级都 ~87%，共同构成 null result。\n      这为 repo-level 实验设置了对比：如果 repo-level TtJ 显著低于 direct cls，\n      则证明 trace generation 在高复杂度下成为瓶颈——而 classification 通过跳过 trace 避开了这个瓶颈。\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-Level Finetuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: \"Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练预测 resolved/unresolved（聚合所有 test）。隔离 granularity 效应。\"\n    expected_results:\n      traj_accuracy: 83.2\n      traj_resolved_f1: 80.5\n      traj_unresolved_f1: 84.8\n      traj_macro_f1: 82.7\n      traj_auc_roc: 0.882\n      per_test_cls_derived_traj_acc: 85.3\n      granularity_effect_pp: 2.1\n      formulation_effect_pp: 0.0\n      combined_effect_pp: 2.1\n      class_balance_resolved_pct: 38.5\n      class_balance_unresolved_pct: 61.5\n    result_rationale: |\n      Trajectory-level 在函数级仍表现合理（83.2% acc）因为 test suites 小（通常 3-8 test cases per problem）。\n      但比 per-test classification 的 derived trajectory accuracy（85.3%）低 2.1pp——\n      这是 granularity 效应：trajectory model 必须一次性从所有 test 的 concatenation 做出判断，\n      而 per-test model 逐个 test 判断后 AND 聚合，降低了每次推理的认知负担。\n      关键发现：formulation effect = 0pp（因为函数级 CLS ≈ CWM），granularity effect = 2.1pp。\n      这完成了 2×2 因子分析（formulation × granularity），显示在函数级只有 granularity 轴有微弱效应。\n      类别不平衡（61.5% unresolved）出现是因为多数 mutation 至少破坏一个 test，\n      导致 unresolved 成为多数类，unresolved_f1 高于 resolved_f1。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: 2×2 Factorial Decomposition — Function-Level\"\n        columns: [\"Formulation\", \"Granularity\", \"Traj Acc\", \"Macro F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Generation (CWM)\", \"Per-test\", \"85.0%*\", 87.5]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"Per-test\", \"85.3%*\", 87.5]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"Trajectory\", \"83.2%\", 82.7]\n        footnotes:\n          - \"*Trajectory accuracy derived from per-test predictions via AND-aggregation\"\n      - name: \"Effect Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Effect\", \"Δ Traj Accuracy (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formulation (Gen→Cls)\", \"0.0 — null at function-level\"]\n          - [\"Granularity (Traj→Per-test)\", \"+2.1\"]\n          - [\"Combined\", \"+2.1\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 4: 2×2 factorial heatmap，formulation axis 无差异，granularity axis 有 ~2pp 效应\"\n    analysis: |\n      在函数级，formulation 效应为零（CLS ≈ CWM），只有 granularity 贡献 2.1pp。\n      这是 best tier 叙事的关键一环：函数级的 2×2 分析为 repo-level 实验提供了 baseline。\n      如果 repo-level 实验显示 formulation 效应从 0 跳到 12+pp，则证明优势是 complexity-dependent 的。\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B → 8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: \"Classification 和 CWM 各扩展到 8B，验证函数级等价性是否随模型规模保持。\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_8b_pass_f1: 89.8\n      cls_8b_fail_f1: 90.4\n      cls_8b_macro_f1: 90.1\n      cls_8b_accuracy: 90.2\n      cwm_8b_pass_f1: 89.5\n      cwm_8b_fail_f1: 90.1\n      cwm_8b_macro_f1: 89.8\n      cwm_8b_accuracy: 89.9\n      gap_8b_macro_f1_pp: 0.3\n      gap_4b_macro_f1_pp: 0.0\n      cls_scaling_gain_pp: 2.6\n      cwm_scaling_gain_pp: 2.3\n      cwm_8b_exact_match: 87.5\n      cwm_8b_unparseable: 0\n    result_rationale: |\n      函数级 CWM 在 4B 已经不触发 failure modes（unparseable=0, exact_match=84%），\n      8B 进一步改善 exact match 到 87.5% 但 pass/fail 准确率提升与 classification 相当。\n      两者在 8B 仍然等价（gap 0.3pp，统计噪声范围内），因为函数级 execution output 短到\n      即使 4B 也能完整生成——增加参数只改善边际 case 的处理。\n      Scaling gain 略有差异（Cls +2.6 vs CWM +2.3）但不显著。\n      这强化了 complexity-dependent 叙事：不是模型太小导致 CWM 差，\n      而是函数级复杂度太低让 CWM 也能 work。gap 只在 repo-level 复杂度下出现。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Scaling Behavior — Function-Level\"\n        columns: [\"Scale\", \"Cls Macro F1\", \"CWM Macro F1\", \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"4B\", 87.5, 87.5, 0.0]\n          - [\"8B\", 90.1, 89.8, 0.3]\n          - [\"Scaling gain\", \"+2.6\", \"+2.3\", \"+0.3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5: 4B vs 8B scaling curve，两条线几乎平行，gap 保持在噪声水平\"\n    analysis: |\n      函数级 scaling 实验排除了 \"CWM 在更大模型上会超越 classification\" 的 reviewer 质疑（至少在函数级）。\n      两种 formulation 的 scaling rate 相似，说明在此复杂度下两者的 learning dynamics 等价。\n      论文应指出：真正的 scaling 差异预期出现在 repo-level——CWM 需要更多参数来处理长 trace，\n      而 classification 因 1-token output 效率更高。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Precision/Recall Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: \"在完整测试集上测量 per-test failure prediction 的 precision/recall，评估诊断信号质量。\"\n    expected_results:\n      fail_precision: 87.6\n      fail_recall: 88.2\n      fail_f1: 87.9\n      pass_precision: 87.4\n      pass_recall: 86.8\n      pass_f1: 87.1\n      false_positive_rate_pct: 8.3\n      false_negative_rate_pct: 11.8\n      failure_localization_exact_match_pct: 78.2\n      precision_at_k1: 89.3\n      precision_at_k3: 85.1\n    result_rationale: |\n      Fail precision 87.6% 和 recall 88.2% 直接来源于 mvp-b-train 的已有指标。\n      新增指标 failure_localization_exact_match（78.2%）衡量每个 problem 是否完整识别了所有 failing tests——\n      低于 per-test F1（87.9%）因为需要所有 test 都判对。但 78% 意味着约 4/5 的 problem \n      能获得完全正确的 diagnostic 信息。FPR 8.3% 足够低（12 次预测 fail 中约 1 次是误报），\n      对 downstream re-repair agent 来说是可接受的误报率。\n      Precision@1（89.3%）表明 top-ranked failing test 几乎总是真实的失败——\n      这对 repair agent 的 \"先修最可能的 failure\" 策略非常有价值。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Diagnostic Signal Quality — Function-Level\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Fail Class\", \"Pass Class\", \"Macro\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Precision\", \"87.6%\", \"87.4%\", \"87.5%\"]\n          - [\"Recall\", \"88.2%\", \"86.8%\", \"87.5%\"]\n          - [\"F1\", \"87.9%\", \"87.1%\", \"87.5%\"]\n      - name: \"Failure Localization\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Exact match (all tests correct)\", \"78.2%\"]\n          - [\"Precision@1\", \"89.3%\"]\n          - [\"False positive rate\", \"8.3%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6: Precision-Recall curve for fail class，AUC 标注，与 random baseline 对比\"\n    analysis: |\n      Per-test prediction 质量支撑 Claim 2：diagnostic signal 足够准确以产生实际价值。\n      78% exact match 意味着大多数情况下 repair agent 获得完全正确的 failing test list。\n      即使不完全正确，部分 diagnostic 信息仍优于无信息（re-repair 实验将验证这一点）。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P-Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: \"按 F2P test count (T=1, T=2, T≥3) 分层 oracle 分析，展示 per-test advantage 集中在 multi-test 实例。\"\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct_instances: 68.7\n      T1_iid_adv_70_85_pct: 2.0\n      T1_block_adv_70_85_pct: 10.9\n      T2_pct_instances: 16.2\n      T2_iid_adv_70_85_pct: 17.5\n      T2_block_adv_70_85_pct: 38.0\n      T3plus_pct_instances: 15.1\n      T3plus_iid_adv_70_85_pct: 26.5\n      T3plus_block_adv_70_85_pct: 45.2\n      weighted_iid_adv_pct: 7.6\n      weighted_block_adv_pct: 19.5\n    result_rationale: |\n      T=1 时 per-test 和 trajectory 对 F2P 部分数学上等价（只有一个 failing test，\n      per-test 预测和 trajectory 预测携带相同信息）——advantage 仅来自 tie-breaking（iid 2%）\n      或 block correlation 效应（10.9%）。\n      T=2 时 advantage 跳升至 17.5%/38.0%：per-test 能区分 \"fails test A only\" vs \"fails both A and B\"，\n      而 trajectory 将两者都折叠为 \"unresolved\"。这种信息增益在 candidate ranking 中产生显著差异。\n      T≥3 时 advantage 最大（26.5%/45.2%）因为 failure pattern 的组合空间增长，\n      per-test 捕获的信息量远超 trajectory-level。\n      Block-correlated advantage 始终显著高于 iid（~2-3×）因为 block 错误结构\n      减少了有效自由度，放大了 per-test 的信息优势。\n      Population-weighted advantage（7.6% iid / 19.5% block）因 T=1 占 68.7% 而被稀释——\n      这是诚实的报告，但也说明：如果 deployment 能 filter 出 multi-F2P instances，\n      per-test 的 ROI 大幅提升。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Per-test Advantage Stratified by F2P Count (Oracle, acc ∈ [70%, 85%])\"\n        columns: [\"F2P Count (T)\", \"% Instances\", \"Adv (i.i.d.)\", \"Adv (Block-corr)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"68.7%\", \"2.0%\", \"10.9%\"]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"16.2%\", \"17.5%\", \"38.0%\"]\n          - [\"T≥3\", \"15.1%\", \"26.5%\", \"45.2%\"]\n          - [\"Weighted\", \"100%\", \"7.6%\", \"19.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 7: Stacked bar chart 按 T 分层的 per-test advantage，iid vs block 双柱对比\"\n      - \"Figure 8: Advantage vs T 的 scatter plot with fitted curve，展示 advantage 随 T 单调递增\"\n    analysis: |\n      分层分析是 Claim 3 的核心结果。它提供了实用决策框架：\n      当 instance 预期有 T≥2 个 failing tests（SWE-bench 中 31.3% 的情况），\n      per-test verification 的 expected advantage 为 20-42%。\n      对于 T=1 instances，per-test 与 trajectory 几乎等价（可以省略 per-test 分解以节省成本）。\n      这个 characterization 比 \"per-test is always better\" 的 overclaim 更有说服力。\n\n  - name: \"Block-Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: \"从训练好的 classification model 的 per-test 预测中测量实际 error correlation 结构。\"\n    expected_results:\n      within_instance_spearman_rho: 0.43\n      within_instance_pearson_r: 0.41\n      between_instance_spearman_rho: 0.028\n      iid_model_rho: 0.0\n      block_model_rho: 1.0\n      n_instances_analyzed: 487\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 4.7\n      correlation_by_T2: 0.49\n      correlation_by_T3: 0.44\n      correlation_by_T4plus: 0.38\n    result_rationale: |\n      Within-instance ρ=0.43 表明预测误差显著正相关：当模型对某个 (code, test_A) 判错时，\n      同一 code 的 test_B 也大概率被判错。这是因为同一 patch 的所有 test 共享相同的代码语义——\n      如果模型误解了 patch 的行为，相关的 test 都会受影响。\n      Between-instance ρ≈0.03 接近零，说明错误是 instance-specific 的（模型没有系统性偏差）。\n      ρ=0.43 处于 iid（ρ=0）和 full block（ρ=1）之间偏向 block 一侧，\n      验证了 oracle 分析中 block-correlation 假设的合理性：\n      block-corr 结果（36-45%）是上界，iid 结果（2-27%）是下界，真实值在两者之间偏上。\n      T=2 时 ρ 最高（0.49）因为只有两个 test 时共享的代码推理几乎完全相同；\n      T≥4 时 ρ 下降到 0.38 因为 test 多样性增加，部分 test 覆盖不同代码路径。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Empirical Error Correlation Structure\"\n        columns: [\"Scope\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Within-instance\", 0.43, \"Substantial positive correlation\"]\n          - [\"Between-instance\", 0.028, \"Near-zero (instance-specific)\"]\n          - [\"i.i.d. model\", 0.0, \"Lower bound\"]\n          - [\"Block-corr model\", 1.0, \"Upper bound\"]\n      - name: \"Correlation by F2P Count\"\n        columns: [\"T\", \"ρ\", \"N instances\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=2\", 0.49, 79]\n          - [\"T=3\", 0.44, 42]\n          - [\"T≥4\", 0.38, 31]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 9: ρ vs T scatter plot with 95% CI bands，叠加 iid (ρ=0) 和 block (ρ=1) reference lines\"\n    analysis: |\n      Block-correlation 验证连接了 oracle 模拟（Claim 3）和训练模型（Claim 1）。\n      ρ≈0.43 意味着 oracle 分析的 block 估计偏乐观但方向正确，iid 估计偏保守。\n      真实的 per-test advantage 落在两个 bound 之间，约 60% 权重偏 block。\n      这一发现独立验证了为什么 per-test 在 multi-F2P instances 上优势如此大：\n      block 错误意味着 trajectory-level 更容易「全错」或「全对」，per-test 则能部分纠正。\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: \"Docker 重新执行 SWE-bench Verified patches，提取 per-test pass/fail labels。500 instances × 16 candidates。\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances_target: 500\n      n_instances_successful: 478\n      n_instances_docker_fail: 22\n      n_candidates_per_instance: 16\n      total_test_executions: 391168\n      avg_total_tests_per_instance: 51.2\n      avg_f2p_tests: 3.0\n      median_f2p_tests: 2\n      avg_p2p_tests: 48.2\n      docker_wall_clock_hours: 19.3\n      n_parallel_containers: 16\n      label_agreement_with_original_pct: 98.5\n      flaky_test_rate_pct: 1.2\n    result_rationale: |\n      478/500 成功率（95.6%）与 SWE-bench Docker 基础设施的已知可靠性一致——\n      22 个失败主要来自 Python 版本不兼容（legacy repos 需要 Python 3.7/3.8）和\n      系统级依赖缺失（C extensions, CUDA）。\n      Average F2P=3.0, median=2 与 SWE-bench Verified 的已知分布一致（mean=3, P75=2, P90=3）。\n      98.5% label agreement 验证了 Docker re-evaluation 的方法论——\n      1.5% 不一致主要来自 flaky tests（1.2%）和环境敏感 assertions（0.3%）。\n      19.3h wall-clock 在 16 并行 container 下合理（每个 instance ~0.65h 包括环境搭建 + 测试执行）。\n      数据集本身是独立于论文 claims 的 resource contribution——\n      它使任何 future work on SWE-bench per-test verification 成为可能。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\"\n        columns: [\"Statistic\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Instances (successful)\", 478]\n          - [\"Candidates per instance\", 16]\n          - [\"Total (instance, candidate, test) triples\", \"391,168\"]\n          - [\"Avg F2P tests per instance\", 3.0]\n          - [\"Median F2P tests\", 2]\n          - [\"Avg P2P tests per instance\", 48.2]\n          - [\"Label agreement with SWE-bench\", \"98.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 10: F2P test count 的 histogram（T=1 到 T=15+），展示长尾分布\"\n    analysis: |\n      数据集构建是 repo-level 实验的先决条件。F2P 分布（median=2, mean=3）\n      意味着约 31% 的 instances 有 T≥2，为 per-test advantage 提供足够的 multi-F2P 样本。\n      P2P 测试很多（avg 48.2）但由于 regression rate ~1%（已知），\n      P2P 对 per-test advantage 贡献极小，论文中应明确说明这一限制。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-Level Classification vs CWM Training\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"在 SWE-bench-PerTest 上 fine-tune Qwen3-4B/8B 做 repo-level per-test classification 和 CWM，评估 complexity-dependent gap。\"\n    expected_results:\n      repo_cls_4b_pass_f1: 80.8\n      repo_cls_4b_fail_f1: 83.2\n      repo_cls_4b_macro_f1: 82.0\n      repo_cls_4b_accuracy: 82.3\n      repo_cls_8b_pass_f1: 83.5\n      repo_cls_8b_fail_f1: 85.5\n      repo_cls_8b_macro_f1: 84.5\n      repo_cls_8b_accuracy: 84.8\n      repo_cwm_4b_macro_f1: 70.5\n      repo_cwm_4b_accuracy: 71.2\n      repo_cwm_4b_unparseable_pct: 15.2\n      repo_cwm_4b_truncated_pct: 7.8\n      repo_cwm_4b_unparseable_or_truncated_pct: 23.0\n      repo_cwm_4b_string_mismatch_pct: 18.5\n      repo_cwm_8b_macro_f1: 73.0\n      repo_cwm_8b_unparseable_or_truncated_pct: 18.5\n      gap_4b_pp: 11.5\n      gap_8b_pp: 11.5\n      func_to_repo_cls_f1_drop_pp: 5.5\n      func_to_repo_cwm_f1_drop_pp: 17.0\n      context_length_median_tokens: 6842\n      context_length_p90_tokens: 14207\n      context_truncation_rate_pct: 8.3\n    result_rationale: |\n      这是论文的 headline result。Classification 从函数级 87.5 下降到 repo 级 82.0（-5.5pp），\n      CWM 从 87.5 暴跌到 70.5（-17.0pp）——gap 从 0pp 扩大到 11.5pp。\n      Classification 的温和下降来自三个因素：(1) repo-level context 更长（median 6.8K tokens vs ~500），\n      attention 稀释降低了对关键代码区域的聚焦；(2) cross-file 依赖增加了推理复杂度；\n      (3) 8.3% 的 cases 因 context 超长被截断。但 classification 只需输出 1 token，\n      这些因素只影响理解，不影响生成。\n      CWM 的剧烈下降（-17pp）有明确的机械解释：\n      - Token-budget exhaustion（15.2%）：repo-level execution traces 动辄数百到数千 tokens，\n        4B 模型的 generation window 不够，trace 被截断导致 systematic false-fail。\n      - String-value prediction errors（18.5%）：repo-level output 包含文件路径、版本号、\n        复杂 stack traces、dict/list 格式化——这些不是语义推理而是 lexical memorization 问题。\n      - 两者合计影响 23% 的预测（unparseable + truncated），在 best tier 范围 [15%, 35%] 内。\n      Classification 完全绕过了这些 failure modes——它从不需要生成 execution output tokens。\n      8B 模型的 gap 仍然 11.5pp（CWM 73.0 vs Cls 84.5），说明 scaling 缓解但不解决 CWM 的结构性缺陷。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Repo-Level — Classification vs CWM (SWE-bench-PerTest)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Formulation\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Macro F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B\", \"Classification\", 80.8, 83.2, 82.0]\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B\", \"CWM Generation\", \"—\", \"—\", 70.5]\n          - [\"Δ (Cls − CWM)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"+11.5\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B\", \"Classification\", 83.5, 85.5, 84.5]\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B\", \"CWM Generation\", \"—\", \"—\", 73.0]\n          - [\"Δ (Cls − CWM)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"+11.5\"]\n      - name: \"Table 11: Complexity-Dependent Gap — Function vs Repo Level\"\n        columns: [\"Level\", \"Cls F1 (4B)\", \"CWM F1 (4B)\", \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Function-level\", 87.5, 87.5, 0.0]\n          - [\"Repo-level\", 82.0, 70.5, 11.5]\n          - [\"Drop\", \"−5.5\", \"−17.0\", \"+11.5\"]\n      - name: \"Table 12: CWM Failure Mode Breakdown — Repo-Level\"\n        columns: [\"Failure Mode\", \"% of Predictions\", \"Explanation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Token-budget exhaustion\", \"15.2%\", \"Trace exceeds generation window\"]\n          - [\"String-value mismatch\", \"18.5%\", \"Correct semantics, wrong surface form\"]\n          - [\"Unparseable output\", \"7.8%\", \"Cannot extract pass/fail from generation\"]\n          - [\"Clean predictions (none)\", \"58.5%\", \"CWM works correctly\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 11: Complexity-dependent gap visualization: 函数级 bar pair (gap≈0) vs repo 级 bar pair (gap=11.5pp)\"\n      - \"Figure 12: CWM failure mode pie chart at repo-level，展示 41.5% 的预测受 failure modes 影响\"\n      - \"Figure 13: F1 vs context length scatter/binned plot，classification 平缓下降，CWM 急剧下降\"\n    analysis: |\n      这是论文的核心实验。Complexity-dependent gap 的 narrative 完全成立：\n      函数级 gap=0（null result），repo-level gap=11.5pp（显著差异）。\n      CWM failure mode breakdown 提供了机械解释——不只是报告数字，而是解释为什么。\n      Table 11 是论文的 headline table，应该出现在 abstract 和 introduction 中。\n      Reviewer concern \"classification is trivially easier\" 被函数级 null result 直接反驳：\n      如果 classification 本质上更简单，函数级也应该有 gap。gap=0 证明差异来自复杂度，不来自任务难度。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-repair Experiment\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: \"给 repair agent per-test failure predictions vs 无 per-test info，在 200 instances 上比较 resolve rate。\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances: 200\n      baseline_resolve_rate_pct: 26.5\n      rerepair_without_diagnostics_resolve_rate_pct: 29.0\n      rerepair_with_diagnostics_resolve_rate_pct: 34.5\n      diagnostic_lift_pp: 5.5\n      blind_rerepair_lift_pp: 2.5\n      n_rerepair_triggered: 89\n      rerepair_success_rate_with_diag_pct: 27.0\n      rerepair_success_rate_without_diag_pct: 14.6\n      p_value_mcnemar: 0.016\n      multi_f2p_diagnostic_lift_pp: 10.8\n      single_f2p_diagnostic_lift_pp: 2.3\n    result_rationale: |\n      Diagnostic lift 5.5pp（在 best tier 范围 [3, 8] 内）来自 per-test predictions 为 repair agent\n      提供了 actionable 的失败定位信息。当 agent 知道 \"test_parse_edge_case fails but test_parse_basic passes\" 时，\n      它可以将修复集中在 edge case 处理逻辑上，而不是盲目重试。\n      Blind re-repair（知道 \"有 test 失败\" 但不知道哪个）仍有 2.5pp 提升，因为重试本身就有价值——\n      但 diagnostic-specific lift（5.5 - 2.5 = 3.0pp 增量，或相对于 blind 的 +5.5pp）\n      证明了 per-test 信息的独特贡献。\n      优势集中在 multi-F2P instances（lift 10.8pp vs single-F2P 2.3pp），\n      与 oracle 分析的预测一致：当有多个 failing tests 时，知道哪些 fail 的信息增益最大。\n      McNemar p=0.016 在 200 样本下达到显著性，虽然样本量有限但足以支撑 proof-of-concept。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 13: Diagnostic Re-repair Results\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Resolve Rate\", \"Δ vs Baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"No re-repair (baseline)\", \"26.5%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Re-repair without diagnostics\", \"29.0%\", \"+2.5 pp\"]\n          - [\"Re-repair with per-test diagnostics\", \"34.5%\", \"+8.0 pp\"]\n          - [\"Diagnostic-specific lift\", \"—\", \"+5.5 pp (p=0.016)\"]\n      - name: \"Table 14: Diagnostic Lift by F2P Count\"\n        columns: [\"F2P Count\", \"% Instances\", \"Diag Lift\", \"Blind Lift\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"69%\", \"+2.3 pp\", \"+1.8 pp\"]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"16%\", \"+8.2 pp\", \"+2.5 pp\"]\n          - [\"T≥3\", \"15%\", \"+10.8 pp\", \"+3.6 pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 14: Grouped bar chart — three conditions (baseline / blind / diagnostic) × stratified by T\"\n    analysis: |\n      Re-repair 实验是 Claim 2 的锚点。5.5pp lift 在统计上显著且实际有意义。\n      Stratification 连接了 Claim 2 和 Claim 3：diagnostic 优势集中在 multi-F2P instances，\n      正是 oracle 分析预测的 \"sweet spot\"。\n      论文应定位为 proof-of-concept（不是 SOTA repair），目标是展示机制而非最优数字。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: \"Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot LLM-as-judge，trajectory 和 per-test 两种模式。作为 Pareto frontier 参考点。\"\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_8b_zs_traj_f1: 67.5\n      qwen_8b_zs_traj_accuracy: 68.3\n      qwen_8b_zs_pertest_macro_f1: 63.8\n      qwen_32b_zs_traj_f1: 73.2\n      qwen_32b_zs_traj_accuracy: 74.1\n      qwen_32b_zs_pertest_macro_f1: 70.5\n      finetuned_4b_cls_macro_f1: 87.5\n      finetuned_4b_cost_per_instance: 0.001\n      qwen_8b_cost_per_instance: 0.003\n      qwen_32b_cost_per_instance: 0.012\n    result_rationale: |\n      Zero-shot LLM judges 大幅低于 fine-tuned classifiers，原因：\n      (1) Execution simulation 在 pretraining 数据中代表性不足——模型能推理代码语义\n      但没有学过系统性地预测 pass/fail outcomes；\n      (2) Zero-shot 缺乏 calibration——模型倾向于过度自信或过度保守，没有训练信号来校准阈值；\n      (3) Per-test zero-shot 更差（63.8% vs 67.5% trajectory）因为需要逐个 test 推理，\n      而没有训练数据教模型如何处理单个 test 的判断。\n      Qwen3-8B zero-shot（67.5%）甚至低于 4B fine-tuned CWM（87.5%），\n      说明 fine-tuning 在此任务上比 8× 参数量更有价值。\n      Qwen3-32B zero-shot（73.2%）仍然远低于 4B fine-tuned classification（87.5%），\n      说明即使 32B 规模的 zero-shot prompting 也无法替代 task-specific fine-tuning。\n      这占据 Pareto frontier 的低效区域：高成本（$0.012）低 accuracy。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 15: Pareto Frontier — Accuracy vs Cost\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Params\", \"Fine-tuned\", \"Macro F1\", \"Cost/Instance\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLM-Judge ZS\", \"8B\", \"No\", \"67.5%\", \"$0.003\"]\n          - [\"LLM-Judge ZS\", \"32B\", \"No\", \"73.2%\", \"$0.012\"]\n          - [\"CWM Gen (func)\", \"4B\", \"Yes\", \"87.5%\", \"$0.002\"]\n          - [\"Cls (func)\", \"4B\", \"Yes\", \"87.5%\", \"$0.001\"]\n          - [\"Cls (func)\", \"8B\", \"Yes\", \"90.1%\", \"$0.002\"]\n          - [\"Cls (repo)\", \"4B\", \"Yes\", \"82.0%\", \"$0.001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 15: Pareto frontier scatter plot (F1 vs cost-per-instance)，fine-tuned classification 占据 optimal 角\"\n    analysis: |\n      LLM-judge baselines 回应两个 reviewer concern：\n      (1) \"Why not just prompt a large model?\" — 因为 32B zero-shot 仍比 4B fine-tuned 差 14pp。\n      (2) \"Is fine-tuning necessary?\" — 是的，task-specific training signal 在结构化预测任务上不可替代。\n      Pareto frontier figure 是论文中最直观的可视化之一。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Majority Voting (K=3)\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: \"Classification model 温度采样 K=3 次取多数票，测试 self-consistency 是否提升 per-test accuracy。\"\n    expected_results:\n      k3_pass_f1: 88.5\n      k3_fail_f1: 89.2\n      k3_macro_f1: 88.9\n      k3_accuracy: 89.0\n      single_pass_macro_f1: 87.5\n      improvement_from_voting_pp: 1.4\n      cost_multiplier: 3.0\n      disagreement_rate_pct: 13.5\n      disagreement_accuracy: 62.3\n    result_rationale: |\n      Majority voting 提供 1.4pp 边际改善（87.5→88.9），但代价是 3× 推理成本。\n      改善小的原因：base classifier 在 87.5% 已经是 well-calibrated 的——\n      大多数预测高置信度（86.5% 的 cases 三次投票一致），self-consistency 只在 13.5% 的\n      边界 cases 上有机会纠正错误，且其中也只有 62.3% 被正确纠正。\n      对比：直接用 8B 模型（+2.6pp, ~2× cost）比 4B majority voting（+1.4pp, 3× cost）更高效。\n      结论：majority voting 是 diminishing returns，model scaling 是更好的 accuracy 提升路径。\n      这是 appendix 级别的 P2 结果。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S1 (Appendix): Majority Voting Results\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Macro F1\", \"Relative Cost\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass (4B)\", \"87.5%\", \"1×\"]\n          - [\"Majority K=3 (4B)\", \"88.9%\", \"3×\"]\n          - [\"Single-pass (8B)\", \"90.1%\", \"~2×\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Appendix 级结果。主要贡献是确认 self-consistency 在此任务上 ROI 低，\n      应优先考虑 model scaling。Disagreement rate 可以作为 confidence proxy 用于 selective abstention。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"45f52b71-ca72-4ad0-bac1-693139d71240","total_cost_usd":0.8901555000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32656,"cache_read_input_tokens":179965,"output_tokens":23618,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32656,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":22718,"cache_read_input_tokens":31438,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12919,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12919},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5478,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005583,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":23618,"cacheReadInputTokens":179965,"cacheCreationInputTokens":32656,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8845725,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"300418e6-f6af-40f0-876a-cfbffb85ff53"}
